A||N||7||FieroMaster88||2.5L Piston Question||||5||
Z||000000||FieroMaster88||06-11-2001||03:27 AM||||Ok, i remember hearing something about being able to use either the 305 or 350 V8 pistons in a 2.5L.  I was just wondering if anyone know if there was any truth to this?  Any advice would be appreciated.  <P>------------------<BR>        <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FieroMaster88.gif">        <BR>James Essar<BR>AOL IM Name: FieroMaster88<BR>88 Coupe 30,000 miles  <IMG SRC="http://cwm.ragesofsanity.com/s/net4/smiling2.gif"> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||KRMFiero||06-11-2001||06:56 AM||||I am 99% sure you can, I have a set of brand new pistons for one of my dukes and i had a old 350 or 305 i took apart and the pistons look identical, I belive that a 350 has a 4" bore and the 2.5 does as well - well on my pistons it says 3.999...<P>Kyle||||reg||1
Z||000002||Brucepts||06-11-2001||09:09 AM||||What about the compression height of the pin? Is that that same?<P>------------------<BR>Advanced Dealer in the Great Material Continuum . . .<BR>Non Fiero Website: <A HREF="http://tractorsport.com" TARGET=_blank>http://tractorsport.com</A> <BR>You can't race a dyno . . .||||reg||1
Z||000003||FieroMaster88||06-11-2001||02:00 PM||||Hmm....well i guess i could have looked up bore sizes and figured it out that way...duh.  Hmmm...that gets me thinking...350 pistons in my 2.5..turbo.  Just a thought<P>------------------<BR>        <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FieroMaster88.gif">        <BR>James Essar<BR>AOL IM Name: FieroMaster88<BR>88 Coupe 30,000 miles  <IMG SRC="http://cwm.ragesofsanity.com/s/net4/smiling2.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||erikred||06-12-2001||03:35 PM||||Keith Black <A HREF="http://www.kb-silvolite.com/silvtoc.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.kb-silvolite.com/silvtoc.htm</A> <BR>list the 350 comp. height as being 1.43", 1.54", or 1.56". They list the 151 as 1.566" or 1.570". Be sure to use 350 rings with 350 pistons, they may be different.<P>||||reg||14
Z||000005||c m west||06-12-2001||03:47 PM||||rings are exactly the same as a 350 - came across this info during a 4 cyl rebuild and a ring was broken, measured the ring, and turned out they were the same measurement as well as part number for the 4 cyl and the 350||||reg||1
Z||000006||FieroMaster88||06-12-2001||04:23 PM||||Sweet...glad to know it.  The connecting rods are different and everythign i believe though.....i wonder if the lifters and push rods are the same.  Does anyone know if they make stronger valve components for the 2.5L?<P>------------------<BR>        <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FieroMaster88.gif">        <BR>James Essar<BR>AOL IM Name: FieroMaster88<BR>88 Coupe 30,000 miles  <IMG SRC="http://cwm.ragesofsanity.com/s/net4/smiling2.gif"> ||||reg||14
Z||000007||85Josh||06-12-2001||10:51 PM||||erikred, I've been looking for a website like that for a while, THANKS!<BR>Fieromaster88, try Modifie's Duke site at <A HREF="http://dukemods.50megs.com/WEB%20PAGE/PAGE1.html" TARGET=_blank>http://dukemods.50megs.com/WEB%20PAGE/PAGE1.html</A> <BR>I think there is some info on using big-block Chevy roller lifters in there somewhere.mrrossum, on the Forum, is doing this.<P>------------------<BR>85 2M4(Lil' Bit)||||reg||1
